yt-dlp EJS in MintVID
====================

These two minified JavaScript files are unmodified release assets from
yt-dlp-ejs 0.8.0:

  https://github.com/yt-dlp/ejs/releases/tag/0.8.0

  yt.solver.core.min.js
    SHA-256 18da6ce0758b416e7ae645084f4f8801f9f9d59d6c477c05eaa0ff94ebd8cc00

  yt.solver.lib.min.js
    SHA-256 c55987fe697e5b9ee18830163f7af85327e9bb5c3e674b969d38c8d205eaa577

The library bundle includes Meriyah 6.1.4 and Astring 1.9.0. Their ISC/MIT
licence texts are preserved in the bundle's leading comment. The solver itself
is released under the Unlicense; the upstream LICENSE is retained here.

The corresponding yt_solver_*_le.c and yt_solver_*_be.c files were generated
from these exact assets with the pinned QuickJS qjsc compiler. MintVID embeds
the correct byte order directly in mrplay; the .js files remain here as the
auditable source inputs and are not release-time sidecars.

Generation used qjsc `-c -s` for the little-endian objects and `-c -s -x` for
the big-endian objects, followed only by renaming the generated C files and
their array symbols to the names in this directory. The two large library
array initializers are mechanically divided into part include files and
reassembled by their small C wrappers; the byte sequences are unchanged.

MintVID evaluates the bytecode inside its embedded QuickJS context. It does
not expose file, process, socket or AmigaOS functions to that context.
